   "summary": "Tech giant Microsoft said on Saturday that it has “restored service” to customers, effectively drawing a close to a massive outage that caused chaos and disrupted public services and business around the world. The outage swept the globe on Thursday, taking the company’s products offline in at least 74 countries and territories across the Americas, Europe, Asia and Africa, according to the monitoring site Downdetector. Microsoft had attributed the disruption to “elevated load” on its infrastructure.",
   "summary_zh": "科技巨头Microsoft于星期六表示，已为客户“恢复服务”，实际上结束了这场造成混乱并扰乱全球公共服务和商业活动的大规模中断。据监测网站Downdetector称，故障于星期四席卷全球，使该公司的产品在美洲、欧洲、亚洲和非洲至少74个国家和地区无法使用。Microsoft曾将此次中断归因于其基础设施“负载过高”。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Tech giant Microsoft said on Saturday that it has “restored service” to customers, effectively drawing a close to a massive outage that caused chaos and disrupted public services and business around the world. “We have completed our efforts to address the underlying issue of the incident and restored service to the remaining impacted customers and regions,” the US-based company said in an X post. The outage swept the globe on Thursday, taking the company’s products offline in at least 74 countries and territories across the Americas, Europe, Asia and Africa, according to the monitoring site Downdetector. Microsoft had attributed the disruption to “elevated load” on its infrastructure. It said the stoppage affected its Outlook email service, as well as Microsoft’s Teams communication platform and the company’s Copilot AI assistant",
