   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Mahanadi Coalfields Limited (MCL), a wholly owned subsidiary of Coal India Limited, on Saturday (November 14, 2026) said it has filed the Red Herring Prospectus (RHP) for the proposed initial public offering. The proposed IPO comprises an offer for sale (OFS) of up to 66.18 crore equity shares by Coal India, representing 10% of its stake in the subsidiary. The issue is estimated to fetch around ₹9,500 crore.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁这些内容。印度煤炭有限公司全资子公司马哈纳迪煤田有限公司（MCL）于周六（2026年11月14日）表示，已为拟议首次公开发行提交了招股说明书（RHP）。此次拟议IPO包括由印度煤炭出售最多6618万股股票（OFS），占其在该子公司所持股份的10%。此次发行预计将筹集约₹9,500 crore。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Mahanadi Coalfields Limited (MCL), a wholly owned subsidiary of Coal India Limited, on Saturday (November 14, 2026) said it has filed the Red Herring Prospectus (RHP) for the proposed initial public offering. The RHP, dated November 13, was filed with the Registrar of Companies (RoC), the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI), the BSE and the NSE, Coal India said in a regulatory filing. The proposed IPO comprises an offer for sale (OFS) of up to 66.18 crore equity shares by Coal India, representing 10% of its stake in the subsidiary. The issue is estimated to fetch around ₹9,500 crore. “The proposed public issue remains subject to receipt of applicable approvals, market conditions and other relevant considerations,” the filing said. The IPO is part of Coal India's efforts to unlock value in its subsidiaries through stake sales and their listing on stock exchanges. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
