   "title": "Kwankwaso’s daughter seeks divorce from Kano gov, offers to refund dowry",
   "url": "https://www.vanguardngr.com/2026/11/kwankwasos-daughter-seeks-divorce-from-kano-gov-offers-to-refund-dowry/",
   "domain": "vanguardngr.com",
   "source": "vanguardngr.com",
   "published": "Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:32:55 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794673975.0,
   "ageDays": 0.05,
   "summary": "The second wife of Kano State Governor, Abba Kabir Yusuf, Zainab Musa Kwankwaso, has filed for divorce at an Upper Area Court in Gudu, Abuja, offering to refund the dowry paid by the governor. Zainab, a daughter of former Kano State Governor Senator Rabiu Musa Kwankwaso, is seeking to dissolve the marriage through Khul’i, an Islamic procedure that allows a woman to seek divorce by returning her dowry or offering compensation.",
   "summary_zh": "卡诺州州长阿巴·卡比尔·尤素福的第二任妻子扎伊纳布·穆萨·夸恩克瓦索，已向阿布贾古杜的一所高级地区法院申请离婚，并表示愿意退还州长支付的聘礼。扎伊纳布是前卡诺州州长、拉布尤·穆萨·夸恩克瓦索参议员的女儿。她正通过伊斯兰教程序“胡利”解除婚姻关系；该程序允许女方通过返还聘礼或提供补偿来申请离婚。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The second wife of Kano State Governor, Abba Kabir Yusuf, Zainab Musa Kwankwaso, has filed for divorce at an Upper Area Court in Gudu, Abuja, offering to refund the dowry paid by the governor. Zainab, a daughter of former Kano State Governor Senator Rabiu Musa Kwankwaso, is seeking to dissolve the marriage through Khul’i, an Islamic procedure that allows a woman to seek divorce by returning her dowry or offering compensation. According to court documents, the court has summoned Governor Yusuf to appear on November 17, 2026, to respond to the suit. In her claim, Zainab cited a breakdown of the marriage, alleging a persistent lack of love, care, affection and emotional connection. She also told the court that efforts to reconcile them had failed and expressed willingness to refund the dowry paid on their wedding day. Zainab married Yusuf on July 29, 2006, and their marriage produced six children. Her divorce suit comes weeks after she reportedly left the Kano Government House for her father’s residence before travelling to Abuja. Comments expressed here do not reflect the opinions of Vanguard newspapers or any employee thereof",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
