   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Congress leader and Leader of the Opposition in the Lok Sabha Rahul Gandhi on Saturday (November 14, 2026) alleged that India is no longer a democracy. “It is important for the democratic movement on the planet that India remains a democracy, and what we have found and proven is that India is actually no longer a democracy,” he said. He further alleged that the Congress had discovered that democracy was destroyed in India in 2014.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁这些内容。印度人民院国会议长兼反对党领袖拉胡尔·甘地于2026年11月14日星期六声称，印度已不再是民主国家。他说：“对地球上的民主运动而言，印度继续保持民主至关重要，而我们的发现和证据表明，印度实际上已不再是民主国家。”他还声称，国大党发现，印度的民主制度在2014年就已遭到摧毁。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Congress leader and Leader of the Opposition in the Lok Sabha Rahul Gandhi on Saturday (November 14, 2026) alleged that India is no longer a democracy. Speaking at the Bharat Summit hosted by the Telangana government here, he asked how an election could be legitimate if, as he claimed, the Election Commission had declared 14 crore voters illegal. “It is important for the democratic movement on the planet that India remains a democracy, and what we have found and proven is that India is actually no longer a democracy,” he said. In 2014, the Congress witnessed a completely new election, with millions of dollars injected into the political system and a completely new type of campaign, he said. He further alleged that the Congress had discovered that democracy was destroyed in India in 2014. Mr. Gandhi, who apologised to foreign delegates who could not attend the Bharat Summit, alleged that they were not allowed to attend the event by the Union government. It gives a sense of what “we are dealing with in India,” he claimed. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
