   "title": "Government secures about US$3bn for Accra-Kumasi Expressway",
   "url": "https://www.myjoyonline.com/government-secures-about-us3bn-for-accra-kumasi-expressway/",
   "domain": "myjoyonline.com",
   "source": "MyJoyOnline（加纳）",
   "published": "Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:01:22 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794513682.0,
   "ageDays": 1.91,
   "summary": "Finance Minister Dr Cassiel Ato Forson says the government has secured about US$3 billion for the construction of the Accra-Kumasi Expressway, with the funds held in a dedicated project account at the Bank of Ghana. “Before actual construction of the Accra-Kumasi Expressway begins, the money is ready. The government has dedicated the Annual Budget Funding Amount (ABFA) from petroleum revenues, together with mineral royalties, to the Accra-Kumasi Expressway project.",
   "summary_zh": "财政部长卡西尔·阿托·福尔松博士表示，政府已为修建阿克拉—库马西高速公路筹集约30亿美元，资金存入加纳银行专门设立的项目账户。“在阿克拉—库马西高速公路正式动工之前，资金已经到位。政府已从石油收入中划拨年度预算资金（ABFA），并连同矿产权利金收入一并指定用于阿克拉—库马西高速公路项目。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Finance Minister Dr Cassiel Ato Forson says the government has secured about US$3 billion for the construction of the Accra-Kumasi Expressway, with the funds held in a dedicated project account at the Bank of Ghana. Presenting the 2027 Budget Statement and Economic Policy to Parliament on Thursday, November 12, 2026, he said the account contained US$2.2 billion and GH¢9 billion as of November 11. “As of yesterday, 11th November 2026, the project account at the Bank of Ghana held US$2.2 billion and GH¢9 billion, together equivalent to about US$3 billion. The money is in the safe custody of the Bank of Ghana,” he said. Dr Forson said the funds had been secured ahead of the commencement of construction, describing the development as the fulfilment of a government commitment. “Before actual construction of the Accra-Kumasi Expressway begins, the money is ready. We promised to secure the financing. We have done so. Promise made, promise fulfilled,” he said. The Finance Minister said detailed feasibility studies, engineering designs, costing, and environmental and social assessments had been completed. He said the engineer’s construction estimate for the 198.7-kilometre, six-lane expressway now stood at US$2.98 billion. According to him, the estimate includes contingencies, supervision, land acquisition and compensation. Dr Forson said the revised estimate was more than US$1 billion below an initial projection of about US$4 billion. The government has issued tenders through an international competitive tendering process, with the exercise expected to be completed by the end of 2026. Dr Forson said the final contract prices would be determined through the competitive process. He added that all contract awards would be subject to commitment control approval and value-for-money assessments, in accordance with procurement and public financial management laws. The government has dedicated the Annual Budget Funding Amount (ABFA) from petroleum revenues, together with mineral royalties, to the Accra-Kumasi Expressway project. The project is expected to connect more than 10 million people. With the tendering process expected to conclude by the end of 2026, the next major step will be the award of contracts and commencement of construction",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "gh"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "cor",
    "eco"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
